---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/barton.css';

const levels = [
	'Phonemic Awareness',
	'Consonants & Short Vowels',
	'Closed & Unit Syllables',
	'Multi-Syllable Words & Vowel Teams',
	'Prefixes & Suffixes',
	'Reasons for Silent-E',
	"Vowel-R's",
	'Advanced Vowel Teams',
	'Influence of Foreign Languages',
	'Latin Roots & Greek Combining Forms',
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="Barton — Trapp Tutoring">
	<h1>The Barton Reading &amp; Spelling System</h1>

	<section class="barton-intro">
		<p>
			The good news is, people with Dyslexia can learn how to spell and read! The Barton Reading
			&amp; Spelling System is a structured literacy program that is Orton-Gillingham influenced. It
			is a multi-sensory, direct, explicit, and sequential program designed for intense
			intervention.
			<a class="phrase-link" href="https://bartonreading.com/">Read about how this Orton-Gillingham based approach works</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="barton-levels" aria-labelledby="barton-levels-heading">
		<h2 id="barton-levels-heading">Overview of Barton Levels</h2>
		<p>
			The Barton system is comprised of ten levels. Most students will start in level one, but I
			will give a screener to help determine the best place to start with each person. It takes
			most students about two to three years to complete all ten levels, and the pace depends on
			the student.
		</p>
		<ol>
			{
				levels.map((name, i) => (
					<li>
						Level {i + 1}: {name}
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ol>
		<p>
			For a more in-depth look at what is taught in each level,
			<a class="phrase-link" href="https://bartonreading.com/faqs/#scope">see what is taught in each level</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
